{"data": {"acceptance": ["When translation is complete and all chunks approved, resolve_source_chunks returns source_kind=translated with translated_text regardless of selected voice language; when translation is absent/incomplete/not-fully-approved it returns source_kind=original; behavior mirrors character_discovery._resolve_discovery_input_chunks; suite green."], "assumptions": ["The change mirrors Character Discovery exactly: translation-complete-and-fully-approved unconditionally selects translated text; the selected Character Voices language no longer influences SOURCE selection.", "'Complete and fully approved' means every original chunk has a non-empty approved translated_text (same predicate Character Discovery uses)."], "created_at": "2026-07-24T19:40:07+00:00", "decision": "pause", "open_questions": ["When a translation is complete and fully approved, should Speech Blocks ALWAYS use the translated text (fully matching Character Discovery, so the selected voice language no longer influences source selection) even if the operator selected the original voice language?"], "planned_paths": ["04_Software/AudioMancer/src/audiomancer/services/speech_blocks_service.py", "04_Software/AudioMancer/tests/test_speech_blocks_service.py"], "reason": "Behavior change to core source selection that re-contracts an Active requirement (REQ-FUNC-e85a7cf0) and 3 tests; one open design question about whether to fully drop the voice-language gate. Risk medium meets policy threshold, so human approval is required before requirement/spec work.", "recommended_responses": ["Yes: always use translated text when translation is complete+approved, mirroring Character Discovery; drop the voice-language gate from source selection. This makes the two operations consistent and always uses the repair-normalized text."], "risk": "medium", "scope": ["IN: speech_blocks_service.resolve_source_chunks() source-selection rule; re-contract the 3 linked tests (test_resolve_source_chunks_uses_original_language_selection, _requires_fully_approved_translation, _uses_approved_translated_language_selection) and update REQ-FUNC-e85a7cf0. OUT: Character Discovery (already correct), Speech Blocks persistence (just delivered), voice/speaker assignment and narrator-language logic, AI logic/prompts, UI."], "source": "User request (chat): use translated text for Speech Blocks once translation is complete and fully approved, matching Character Discovery; translated text is also repair-normalized.", "understanding": "Speech Blocks currently selects its source text via resolve_source_chunks() keyed on the selected Character Voices language (original vs translated target), only using translation when that language is selected. Character Discovery already keys purely on translation being complete and every chunk approved (_resolve_discovery_input_chunks). This change makes Speech Blocks consistent: when a translation exists, is complete, and every chunk is approved, use the translated (repair-normalized) text as the source regardless of the selected voice language; otherwise use the original chunking text."}, "event": "alignment.recorded", "time": "2026-07-24T19:40:07+00:00"}
